  "description": "<p>Logo of Scythian Assianism (Russian: Ассианство, <i>Assianstvo</i>), known among the Ossetians as <i>Uatsdin</i> (Ossetian: Уацдин, lit. \"True Faith\"). Scythian folk religion was traditionally practised by the Ossetians and has been nationally revived since the 1980s. The religion has also been adopted by some among the Russians and Ukrainians as a pan-Indo-European faith. The symbol, called th",
